 "answer": "**Yes, the haze is bad in KL today, with readings in the \"unhealthy\" range.** This is based on the latest reports I found, dated Saturday 17 October.\n\n- **Latest reading (9.30am):** Cheras in KL recorded an API of 162 and Batu Muda 159, and Putrajaya also hit 162 (The Edge, Bernama). Nationwide, 24 areas were unhealthy, with Pasir Gudang, Johor highest at 196.\n- **Nearby areas:** Klang was at 171, Petaling Jaya and Shah Alam at 169, and Nilai at 173.\n- **Trend:** Conditions have been poor for several days. Reports from 14–16 October also had KL and Selangor stations in the unhealthy range. On 16 October, Pasir Gudang briefly reached 207, which is \"very unhealthy\" (Malay Mail).\n- **What the numbers mean:** API 101–200 is unhealthy, 201–300 is very unhealthy, and above 300 is hazardous. KL is in the unhealthy band, not the worst one.\n\n**Precautions:**\n- Limit prolonged outdoor activity and exercise, especially for children, older people, pregnant women, and anyone with asthma or heart or lung conditions.\n- Wear a well-fitted N95 or KN95 mask outdoors. Surgical masks don't filter fine particles well.\n- Keep windows closed and run an air purifier or air-conditioning on recirculate if you have one.\n\nReadings change hourly. You can check the live API on the Department of Environment's APIMS site or the MyIPU app.",
